vents (horizontal bar, parallel bars, long horse, side horse) and three track &amp; field events (100 yards, long jump, shot put). The event was dominated by German-speaking gymnasts, who took the first seven places, led by Austrian " [:a {:href "/athletes/29389"} "Julius Lenhart"] ", who represented the Philadelphia Turngemeinde in 1904. The first native-born US gymnast was eighth-placed " [:a {:href "/athletes/31295"} "John Bissinger"] ". " [:a {:href "/athletes/31445"} "Otto Steffen"] " was an American who finished sixth, but he had been born in Germany, came to the US in 1890, and was naturalized in 1900."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Points"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/29389"} "Julius Lenhart"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/USA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/USA.png"}] "USA"]] [:td {} "69.80"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/30323"} "Wilhelm Weber"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/GER"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/GER.png"}] "GER"]] [:td {} "69.10"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "3"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/31044"} "Adolf Spinnler"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/GER"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/GER.png"}] "GER"]] [:td {} "67.99"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Bronze"} "Bronze"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "4"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/30282"} "Ernst Mohr"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/GER"} [:img {:style "padd